meta {
  name: Register Duplicate Email (409)
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "email": "{{testEmail}}",
    "password": "{{testPassword}}",
    "name": "Bruno Tester"
  }
}

docs {
  Re-runs the Register body after that account exists. Expect 409 with
  {"error": "That email is already registered"}.

  A 500 here is a real failure, not a cosmetic one: it means the unique-index
  violation is not being caught, and the handler is doing a select-then-insert
  somewhere instead of letting the database decide. That pattern IS the race.
}
